Subject: Record per-instruction coverage and the never-executed ranges

What this does
  Marks each instruction the interpreter executes in a bitmap and dumps the
  never-executed instruction ranges as `U` lines, with a `V` summary of
  instructions seen and covered.

Why we need it
  Decision 5 compiles code the profile never saw to a single deopt branch, so
  the compiler must know which instructions never ran. Nothing in the profile
  said so.

What it adds
  `JSAotProfFunc.cov` and the `V`/`U` lines; `profmerge.py` merges them,
  intersecting the uncommon ranges so a range is uncommon only if no session
  reached it.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

